@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `usca-operation-of-statutes`

-- Tests of usca-operation-of-statutes.l4.  Each expected value is decided from the section cited above the assertion.  A failing assertion is a finding.

GIVEN order IS A NUMBER
      chapter IS A NUMBER
      even IS A BOOLEAN
      notToPrevail IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Amending statute`
`a statute` order chapter even notToPrevail MEANS
    `Amending statute` WITH
        `order of enactment` IS order
        `chapter number` IS chapter
        `enacted in the even-numbered year of a two-year regular session` IS even
        `says expressly that it is not to prevail` IS notToPrevail


§ `Gov. Code § 9606: repeal at any time, except where vested rights would be impaired`

#ASSERT `a statute may be repealed` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`a statute may be repealed` TRUE)

§ `Gov. Code § 9607(a): no revival by repeal of the repealing statute without express words`

#ASSERT `a repealed statute is revived by the repeal of the statute that repealed it` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a repealed statute is revived by the repeal of the statute that repealed it` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a repealed statute is revived by the repeal of the statute that repealed it` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a repealed statute is revived by the repeal of the statute that repealed it` FALSE FALSE)

§ `Gov. Code § 9607(b): a later statute chaptered before the date of termination revives the law when it becomes operative`

#ASSERT `the day a terminated or repealed law is revived by a later statute chaptered on` (YMD 2026 12 30) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a terminated or repealed law is revived by a later statute chaptered on` (YMD 2026 6 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT `the day a terminated or repealed law is revived by a later statute chaptered on` (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day a terminated or repealed law is revived by a later statute chaptered on` (YMD 2027 1 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2027 1 1) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the day a terminated or repealed law is revived by a later statute chaptered on` (YMD 2027 3 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2027 7 1) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The day the later statute becomes operative can be before or after the termination date; the text revives 'when the later enacted statute becomes operative'.
#ASSERT `the day a terminated or repealed law is revived by a later statute chaptered on` (YMD 2026 5 1) (YMD 2026 12 31) (YMD 2026 11 1) EQUALS JUST (YMD 2026 11 1)

§ `Gov. Code § 9608: termination of a criminal law does not bar punishment of an act already committed`

#ASSERT NOT (`the termination or suspension of a criminal law bars indictment, information and punishment` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT `the termination or suspension of a criminal law bars indictment, information and punishment` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `the termination or suspension of a criminal law bars indictment, information and punishment` FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9608 speaks of an act already committed in violation of the law terminated or suspended; it does not say what follows for an act that was not committed in violation of the law before it ended"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the termination or suspension of a criminal law bars indictment, information and punishment` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9608 speaks of an act already committed in violation of the law terminated or suspended; it does not say what follows for an act that was not committed in violation of the law before it ended"

§ `Gov. Code § 9609: a statute amending a section of a repealed statute is void`

#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 9609 makes a statute amending a section of a repealed statute void` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 9609 makes a statute amending a section of a repealed statute void` FALSE)

§ `Gov. Code § 9610: fixing a salary is not an appropriation`

#ASSERT NOT (`a statute fixing the salary of a State officer or employee is an appropriation of money for it`)
#ASSERT `the salary fixed by statute shall be paid` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the salary fixed by statute shall be paid` FALSE)

§ `Gov. Code § 9611: a temporarily suspended or modified law is not repealed, and has its full force again after the temporary provision`

#ASSERT NOT (`a law temporarily suspended or modified is deemed repealed`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the original provision has its full force again on the day` (YMD 2026 6 1) `after a temporary provision effective through` (YMD 2026 12 31))
#ASSERT NOT (`the original provision has its full force again on the day` (YMD 2026 12 31) `after a temporary provision effective through` (YMD 2026 12 31))
#ASSERT `the original provision has its full force again on the day` (YMD 2027 1 1) `after a temporary provision effective through` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT `the original provision has its full force again on the day` (YMD 2030 1 1) `after a temporary provision effective through` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT (`the original provision has its full force again on the day` (YMD 2026 12 30) `after a temporary provision effective through` (YMD 2026 12 31))

§ `Gov. Code § 9605(a): amendment is not repeal and reenactment`

#ASSERT `the day a provision of an amended section is considered to have been enacted` `unaltered by the amendment` (YMD 1999 5 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 1999 5 1)
#ASSERT `the day a provision of an amended section is considered to have been enacted` `new in the amendment` (YMD 1999 5 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a provision of an amended section is considered to have been enacted` `omitted by the amendment` (YMD 1999 5 1) (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9605(a)(1) treats an omitted provision as repealed at the time of the amendment, not as enacted then"
#ASSERT `the day a provision of an amended section is considered to have been repealed` `omitted by the amendment` (YMD 2026 3 10) EQUALS (YMD 2026 3 10)
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a provision of an amended section is considered to have been repealed` `unaltered by the amendment` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9605(a)(1) says an amended section is not considered repealed and reenacted, and treats only the omitted provisions as repealed"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the day a provision of an amended section is considered to have been repealed` `new in the amendment` (YMD 2026 3 10) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9605(a)(1) treats the new provisions as enacted at the time of the amendment, not as repealed"
#ASSERT NOT (`an amended section is considered repealed and reenacted in the amended form`)
-- § 9605(a)(2): the later act decides whether a portion stands.  Earlier act has it and a later one omits it: omitted deliberately.  Earlier omits and later restores: restored deliberately.
#ASSERT NOT (`a portion stands after successive acts of one session amend the same section` (LIST TRUE, FALSE))
#ASSERT `a portion stands after successive acts of one session amend the same section` (LIST FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `a portion stands after successive acts of one session amend the same section` (LIST TRUE, FALSE, TRUE)
#ASSERT `a portion stands after successive acts of one session amend the same section` (LIST TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`a portion stands after successive acts of one session amend the same section` (LIST FALSE))
#ASSERT NOT (`a portion stands after successive acts of one session amend the same section` (LIST FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE))
#ASSERT `a portion stands after successive acts of one session amend the same section` (LIST TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `a portion stands after successive acts of one session amend the same section` EMPTY BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9605(a)(2) speaks of a section amended by two or more acts; no act was given"

§ `Gov. Code § 9605(b): two statutes of one session amend the same section`

-- (1) the statute enacted last prevails absent an express contrary provision in it; (2) the statute with the higher chapter number prevails absent an express contrary provision in it.
-- Both point at the second statute: enacted last (order 2) and the higher chapter (20 over 10).
#ASSERT `the statute that prevails when two statutes of one session amend the same section` (`a statute` 1 10 FALSE FALSE) (`a statute` 2 20 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the second statute`
-- Both point at the first statute: enacted last (order 2 is the first argument) and the higher chapter.
#ASSERT `the statute that prevails when two statutes of one session amend the same section` (`a statute` 2 20 FALSE FALSE) (`a statute` 1 10 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the first statute`
-- (1) points at the second (enacted last), (2) at the first (chapter 10 over 5): the text does not rank them.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the statute that prevails when two statutes of one session amend the same section` (`a statute` 1 10 FALSE FALSE) (`a statute` 2 5 FALSE FALSE) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9605(b)(1) and (b)(2) point at different statutes, and the text does not say which presumption governs"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the statute that prevails when two statutes of one session amend the same section` (`a statute` 2 5 FALSE FALSE) (`a statute` 1 10 FALSE FALSE) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9605(b)(1) and (b)(2) point at different statutes, and the text does not say which presumption governs"
-- The statute enacted last says expressly that it is not to prevail: (1) is closed; (2) points at the first (chapter 10 over 5).
#ASSERT `the statute that prevails when two statutes of one session amend the same section` (`a statute` 1 10 FALSE FALSE) (`a statute` 2 5 FALSE TRUE) EQUALS `the first statute`
-- The statute with the higher chapter number says expressly that it is not to prevail: (2) is closed; (1) points at the second.
#ASSERT `the statute that prevails when two statutes of one session amend the same section` (`a statute` 1 10 FALSE TRUE) (`a statute` 2 5 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the second statute`
-- Each of the two says it is not to prevail: no presumption open.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the statute that prevails when two statutes of one session amend the same section` (`a statute` 1 10 FALSE TRUE) (`a statute` 2 5 FALSE TRUE) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9605(b) gives no presumption when the statute enacted last, and the statute with the higher chapter number, each expressly provide that they are not to prevail, or when the chapter ranks are equal"
-- The even-numbered year is deemed a higher chapter number: first enacted in the even year with chapter 40, second in the odd year with chapter 900: (2) points at the first, (1) at the second.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the statute that prevails when two statutes of one session amend the same section` (`a statute` 3 40 TRUE FALSE) (`a statute` 4 900 FALSE FALSE) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9605(b)(1) and (b)(2) point at different statutes, and the text does not say which presumption governs"
-- Second in the even year with the lower chapter 3, first in the odd year with chapter 50: both point at the second.
#ASSERT `the statute that prevails when two statutes of one session amend the same section` (`a statute` 1 50 FALSE FALSE) (`a statute` 2 3 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS `the second statute`
-- Equal chapter numbers in years of the same kind: (2) is not open; (1) decides.
#ASSERT `the statute that prevails when two statutes of one session amend the same section` (`a statute` 1 7 FALSE FALSE) (`a statute` 2 7 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the second statute`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the statute that prevails when two statutes of one session amend the same section` (`a statute` 1 7 FALSE FALSE) (`a statute` 2 7 FALSE TRUE) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9605(b) gives no presumption when the statute enacted last, and the statute with the higher chapter number, each expressly provide that they are not to prevail, or when the chapter ranks are equal"
-- The same order of enactment: (1) has no statute enacted last.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the statute that prevails when two statutes of one session amend the same section` (`a statute` 2 7 FALSE FALSE) (`a statute` 2 9 FALSE FALSE) BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 9605(b)(1) turns on which statute is enacted last; two statutes with the same order of enactment have none"
-- The chapter rank as § 9605(b)(2) deems it: a statute of the even-numbered year is higher than any of the odd-numbered year.
#ASSERT `the chapter rank of` (`a statute` 1 50 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 50
#ASSERT `the chapter rank of` (`a statute` 1 50 TRUE FALSE) EQUALS 1000050
#ASSERT `the chapter rank of` (`a statute` 1 999999 FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 999999
#ASSERT `the chapter rank of` (`a statute` 1 3 TRUE FALSE) GREATER THAN `the chapter rank of` (`a statute` 1 999999 FALSE FALSE)

§ `References and continuations`

-- Gov. Code § 2: substantially the same as an existing statutory provision on the same subject.  Civ. Code § 5: existing statutes or the common law.  Code Civ. Proc. § 5: existing statutes.
#ASSERT `the section construes a provision of` `the Government Code` `as a restatement and continuation, given that it is substantially the same as an existing statute:` TRUE `and as the common law:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the section construes a provision of` `the Government Code` `as a restatement and continuation, given that it is substantially the same as an existing statute:` FALSE `and as the common law:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the section construes a provision of` `the Government Code` `as a restatement and continuation, given that it is substantially the same as an existing statute:` FALSE `and as the common law:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the section construes a provision of` `the Civil Code` `as a restatement and continuation, given that it is substantially the same as an existing statute:` TRUE `and as the common law:` FALSE
#ASSERT `the section construes a provision of` `the Civil Code` `as a restatement and continuation, given that it is substantially the same as an existing statute:` FALSE `and as the common law:` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the section construes a provision of` `the Civil Code` `as a restatement and continuation, given that it is substantially the same as an existing statute:` FALSE `and as the common law:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the section construes a provision of` `the Code of Civil Procedure` `as a restatement and continuation, given that it is substantially the same as an existing statute:` TRUE `and as the common law:` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the section construes a provision of` `the Code of Civil Procedure` `as a restatement and continuation, given that it is substantially the same as an existing statute:` FALSE `and as the common law:` TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`the section construes a provision of` `the Code of Civil Procedure` `as a restatement and continuation, given that it is substantially the same as an existing statute:` FALSE `and as the common law:` FALSE)
#ASSERT `Gov. Code § 9604 deems a reference to be a reference to the restatements and continuations` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 9604 deems a reference to be a reference to the restatements and continuations` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 9604 deems a reference to be a reference to the restatements and continuations` FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`Gov. Code § 9604 deems a reference to be a reference to the restatements and continuations` FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT `a reference to a portion of the Government Code or of another law of this State applies to its amendments and additions, whenever made`
#ASSERT `the general provisions of the Government Code govern the construction of the code` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the general provisions of the Government Code govern the construction of the code` TRUE)

§ `Retroactivity, pending proceedings, accrued rights, limitation periods`

#ASSERT `a part of the Civil Code or the Code of Civil Procedure is retroactive` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a part of the Civil Code or the Code of Civil Procedure is retroactive` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the section protects an action, proceeding or accrued right from the code` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the section protects an action, proceeding or accrued right from the code` FALSE)
#ASSERT `procedure taken after the code took effect in a proceeding begun before must conform to the code` `the Government Code` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`procedure taken after the code took effect in a proceeding begun before must conform to the code` `the Government Code` FALSE)
#ASSERT `procedure taken after the code took effect in a proceeding begun before must conform to the code` `the Code of Civil Procedure` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`procedure taken after the code took effect in a proceeding begun before must conform to the code` `the Code of Civil Procedure` FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `procedure taken after the code took effect in a proceeding begun before must conform to the code` `the Civil Code` TRUE BECAUSE "Civ. Code § 6 says a proceeding begun before the code took effect is not affected by it, and has no sentence on whether later procedure conforms"
-- CCP § 9: the time that has already run is part of the time the code prescribes.  A one-year (365-day) limitation begun on 1 January 1873... here begun 100 days before the code took effect leaves 265.
#ASSERT `days left of a limitation that began to run before the code took effect` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 4 11) 365 EQUALS 265
#ASSERT `days left of a limitation that began to run before the code took effect` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 2) 90 EQUALS 89
#ASSERT `days left of a limitation that began to run before the code took effect` (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) 365 EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `days left of a limitation that began to run before the code took effect` (YMD 2026 4 11) (YMD 2026 1 1) 365 BECAUSE "Code Civ. Proc. § 9 speaks of a limitation that has begun to run before the code goes into effect; this one did not"
#ASSERT REFUSED `days left of a limitation that began to run before the code took effect` (YMD 2026 1 1) (YMD 2026 1 1) 365 BECAUSE "Code Civ. Proc. § 9 speaks of a limitation that has begun to run before the code goes into effect; this one did not"

§ `Offices, common law, repeal by the codes`

#ASSERT `a holder of an office under a repealed act continues to hold it under Gov. Code § 3` TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `a holder of an office under a repealed act continues to hold it under Gov. Code § 3` FALSE BECAUSE "Gov. Code § 3 speaks of offices that the code continues; it does not say what becomes of the holder of an office the code does not continue"
#ASSERT `a holder of an office under a repealed Act continues to hold it under Code Civ. Proc. § 6 and § 7` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a holder of an office under a repealed Act continues to hold it under Code Civ. Proc. § 6 and § 7` FALSE)
#ASSERT `the common law of England is the rule of decision` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`the common law of England is the rule of decision` TRUE)
#ASSERT `an earlier statute, law or rule remains in force` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`an earlier statute, law or rule remains in force` TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT REFUSED `an earlier statute, law or rule remains in force` FALSE TRUE BECAUSE "Civ. Code § 20 and Code Civ. Proc. § 18 repeal earlier law in all cases provided for by the Code; they do not say what becomes of earlier law on a matter the Code does not provide for"
#ASSERT REFUSED `an earlier statute, law or rule remains in force` FALSE FALSE BECAUSE "Civ. Code § 20 and Code Civ. Proc. § 18 repeal earlier law in all cases provided for by the Code; they do not say what becomes of earlier law on a matter the Code does not provide for"
#ASSERT NOT (`the repeal by the code revives a former law that was repealed before`)
#ASSERT `the repeal by the Code of Civil Procedure affects a private statute` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the repeal by the Code of Civil Procedure affects a private statute` FALSE)

§ `Civ. Code § 23 to § 23.6: the four 1872 codes`

#ASSERT REFUSED `the day each of the four 1872 codes is construed as having been passed` BECAUSE "Civ. Code § 23 says each of the four codes is construed as passed on the first day of the 1872 session, and no deposited section gives the date of that day"
#ASSERT `Civ. Code § 23.1 makes the provision of a law passed at the 1872 session prevail over the code provision` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`Civ. Code § 23.1 makes the provision of a law passed at the 1872 session prevail over the code provision` FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`one of the four 1872 codes prevails over another by having been passed later`)
#ASSERT `the provision that prevails when units conflict` `titles` `the subject matter of the first provision's unit` EQUALS `the first statute`
#ASSERT `the provision that prevails when units conflict` `titles` `the subject matter of the second provision's unit` EQUALS `the second statute`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the provision that prevails when units conflict` `titles` `the subject matter of neither` BECAUSE "Civ. Code §§ 23.3 to 23.5 make each provision prevail on matters arising out of the subject matter of its own title, chapter or article; they do not say which prevails on a matter arising out of neither"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the provision that prevails when units conflict` `titles` `the subject matter of both` BECAUSE "Civ. Code §§ 23.3 to 23.5 make each provision prevail on matters arising out of the subject matter of its own title, chapter or article; they do not say which prevails on a matter arising out of both"
#ASSERT `the provision that prevails when units conflict` `chapters of the same title` `the subject matter of the first provision's unit` EQUALS `the first statute`
#ASSERT `the provision that prevails when units conflict` `chapters of the same title` `the subject matter of the second provision's unit` EQUALS `the second statute`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the provision that prevails when units conflict` `chapters of the same title` `the subject matter of neither` BECAUSE "Civ. Code §§ 23.3 to 23.5 make each provision prevail on matters arising out of the subject matter of its own title, chapter or article; they do not say which prevails on a matter arising out of neither"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the provision that prevails when units conflict` `chapters of the same title` `the subject matter of both` BECAUSE "Civ. Code §§ 23.3 to 23.5 make each provision prevail on matters arising out of the subject matter of its own title, chapter or article; they do not say which prevails on a matter arising out of both"
#ASSERT `the provision that prevails when units conflict` `articles of the same chapter` `the subject matter of the first provision's unit` EQUALS `the first statute`
#ASSERT `the provision that prevails when units conflict` `articles of the same chapter` `the subject matter of the second provision's unit` EQUALS `the second statute`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the provision that prevails when units conflict` `articles of the same chapter` `the subject matter of neither` BECAUSE "Civ. Code §§ 23.3 to 23.5 make each provision prevail on matters arising out of the subject matter of its own title, chapter or article; they do not say which prevails on a matter arising out of neither"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the provision that prevails when units conflict` `articles of the same chapter` `the subject matter of both` BECAUSE "Civ. Code §§ 23.3 to 23.5 make each provision prevail on matters arising out of the subject matter of its own title, chapter or article; they do not say which prevails on a matter arising out of both"
-- § 23.6: the section last in numerical order prevails, unless that is inconsistent with the meaning of the chapter or article.
#ASSERT `the section that prevails, the first being` 10 `and the second` 12 `and given that` FALSE EQUALS `the second statute`
#ASSERT `the section that prevails, the first being` 12 `and the second` 10 `and given that` FALSE EQUALS `the first statute`
#ASSERT `the section that prevails, the first being` 23.5 `and the second` 23.6 `and given that` FALSE EQUALS `the second statute`
#ASSERT `the section that prevails, the first being` 22.2 `and the second` 22 `and given that` FALSE EQUALS `the first statute`
#ASSERT REFUSED `the section that prevails, the first being` 10 `and the second` 12 `and given that` TRUE BECAUSE "Civ. Code § 23.6 makes the section last in numerical order prevail unless that is inconsistent with the meaning of the chapter or article, and does not say which section prevails then"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the section that prevails, the first being` 10 `and the second` 10 `and given that` FALSE BECAUSE "Civ. Code § 23.6 turns on numerical order, and two sections with one number have none"
